    "source_detail": "Finstack Quant canonical pricing calculation on deterministic synthetic market inputs Canonical typed market inputs are supplied directly; the pricing tolerance contract is preserved. Re-blessed 2026-06-16: expected outputs recaptured from the current canonical Python golden runner for this formula self-test after deterministic pricing output drift; no external benchmark source is asserted by this fixture. 2026-10-11 contractual-input remediation: explicit synthetic published monthly CPI follows the existing log-linear projection knots (300 before the base date), with assumed releases on the following month 15th. An explicit zero ratio-volatility surface selects this deterministic fixture. Nominal projected cashflows now use the existing nominal USD-OIS discount curve, rather than the real USD-TIPS curve. NPV and central 1 bp nominal DV01 independently verified by summing actual/365 coupon periods times monthly-interpolated lagged CPI and log-linear nominal discount factors; zero volatility makes the terminal floor deterministic. Yield-derived metrics remain internal regression anchors.",
